      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order. The FDA-approved label for amlodipine sets the maximum adult dose at 10 mg once daily, so 50 mg is not within the label maximum. I can't verify the claim that it is, and it conflicts with the labeling I know.\n\nA single 50 mg dose carries a real risk of severe hypotension and shock. Because amlodipine has a long half-life, that effect could last days.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter 5 mg or 10 mg once daily.** Tell me which and I'll enter it right away.\n- **Talk to pharmacy or the attending.** If you have a specific clinical reason for a dose above the label maximum, they can review it. Their sign-off and any override should go through your hospital's usual high-dose process.\n- **Check the source.** If a reference shows 50 mg, please look again. It may be a different drug or a different unit."
      }
